---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  "<p>Koakademy includes an accounting and cashiering subsystem engineered for educational billing. It handles complex fee calculations, installment plans, cashier counter collections, and automated Statement of Account (SOA) generation.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Tuition Assessment Architecture</h2>\n<pre><code>┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        Enrollment Assessment                           │\n└───────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                    │\n       ┌────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┐\n       ▼                            ▼                            ▼\n┌──────────────┐             ┌──────────────┐             ┌──────────────┐\n│ Lecture Unit │             │  Laboratory  │             │Miscellaneous │\n│    Rates     │             │  Unit Rates  │             │&amp; Fixed Fees  │\n└──────┬───────┘             └──────┬───────┘             └──────┬───────┘\n       │                            │                            │\n       └────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┘\n                                    ▼\n                     ┌─────────────────────────────┐\n                     │    Gross Tuition Total      │\n                     └──────────────┬──────────────┘\n                                    │\n                                    ▼\n                     ┌─────────────────────────────┐\n                     │    Discounts &amp; Vouchers     │\n                     │  (Academic, Sibling, Aid)   │\n                     └──────────────┬──────────────┘\n                                    │\n                                    ▼\n                     ┌─────────────────────────────┐\n                     │     Net Assessment Due      │\n                     └──────────────┬──────────────┘\n                                    │\n                     ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐\n                     ▼                             ▼\n             ┌──────────────┐              ┌──────────────┐\n             │  Full Cash   │              │ Installment  │\n             │ Payment Plan │              │ Schedule     │\n             └──────────────┘              └──────────────┘\n</code></pre>\n<hr>\n<h2>Fee Structures &amp; Pricing Models</h2>\n<h3>1. Tuition Per Unit (<code>FeeScheduleVersion</code>)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Lecture Units:</strong> Standard classroom instruction rate billed per lecture credit unit.</li>\n<li><strong>Laboratory Units:</strong> Higher rates reflecting specialized facility consumption (e.g., computer, engineering, culinary, and nursing laboratories).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Miscellaneous &amp; Auxiliary Fees (<code>AdditionalFee</code>)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Standard Institutional Fees:</strong> Registration, Library, Athletic, Medical/Dental, Cultural, and Guidance fees.</li>\n<li><strong>Course-Specific Fees:</strong> Clinical affiliation fees, culinary ingredients fees, computer laboratory maintenance, and graduation fees.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Discounts &amp; Financial Assistance (<code>EnrollmentDiscount</code>)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Automated Sibling Discounts:</strong> Sibling detection automatically applies graduated discounts (e.g., 10% off tuition for second child, 20% for third child).</li>\n<li><strong>Academic Merit Grants:</strong> Top-ranking incoming students receive full or partial tuition waivers tied to maintaining a minimum GWA.</li>\n<li><strong>Employee Dependents:</strong> Tuition privileges for faculty and administrative staff children.</li>\n<li><strong>Manual Voucher Posting:</strong> Bursar authorization to post external sponsorship checks (e.g., government tertiary education subsidies, NGO scholarships).</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Installment Payment Plans</h2>\n<p>Institutions can offer structured payment terms without manual ledger tracking (<code>StudentTuitionInstallment</code>):</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Term / Stage</th>\n<th>Typical Allocation</th>\n<th>Enforcement Gate</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Downpayment</strong></td>\n<td>20% of net tuition</td>\n<td>Mandatory for enrollment confirmation and class roster inclusion.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Prelim Exam</strong></td>\n<td>20% of net tuition</td>\n<td>Required for prelim exam permit issuance.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Midterm Exam</strong></td>\n<td>20% of net tuition</td>\n<td>Required for midterm exam permit issuance.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Prefinal Exam</strong></td>\n<td>20% of net tuition</td>\n<td>Required for prefinal exam permit issuance.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Final Exam</strong></td>\n<td>Remaining balance</td>\n<td>Required for final exam permit and grade release.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>Cashier Point-of-Sale (POS) Workflow</h2>\n<p>The Cashier Module provides a keyboard-optimized counter interface designed for high-throughput payment processing during peak enrollment rushes:</p>\n<pre><code>┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [CASHIER REGISTER]                     Terminal: POS-1│\n│                                                        │\n│  Student Lookup: [ 2026-00412 ]  JUAN DELA CRUZ        │\n│  Program: BS Information Technology                    │\n│  Outstanding Balance: ₱14,500.00                       │\n│                                                        │\n│  Allocations:                                          │\n│  [x] Midterm Installment                   ₱5,000.00   │\n│  [x] Laboratory Fee Deficiency             ₱1,200.00   │\n│                                                        │\n│  Total Amount Due:                         ₱6,200.00   │\n│  Payment Method: [ Cash / Cheque / Card / GCash ]      │\n│  Amount Tendered: ₱7,000.00      Change: ₱800.00       │\n│                                                        │\n│  [ PRINT OFFICIAL RECEIPT (OR # 2026-9841) ]           │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Instant Receipt Generation:</strong> Prints standardized Official Receipts (OR) with automatic breakdown of tuition, VAT (if applicable), and auxiliary fees.</li>\n<li><strong>Multi-Tender Support:</strong> Accepts split payments across Cash, Cheque, Bank Deposit, and digital payment providers.</li>\n<li><strong>Daily Drawer Balancing:</strong> End-of-shift reconciliation reporting cash collections, cheques received, and electronic settlements.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Statements of Account (SOA)</h2>\n<p>Koakademy generates official Statements of Account on demand for students, parents, and corporate sponsors (<code>StatementOfAccountIssuance</code>):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Live Balances:</strong> Real-time ledger entries showing every debit assessment, payment receipt, and applied adjustment.</li>\n<li><strong>Cryptographic Verification:</strong> Each SOA is stamped with a unique verification token and QR code, confirming authenticity when submitted for educational loans or visa applications.</li>\n<li><strong>Automated Delivery:</strong> Automated scheduled jobs can broadcast electronic statements to registered parent emails prior to upcoming exam periods.</li>\n</ul>\n"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Financial Management, Billing & Cashiering"
  path="/docs/features/finance-cashiering"
  description="Automated tuition fee assessments, installment schedules, statements of account, cashiering POS, and financial audits."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
